  "data": [
    {
      "abstract": "THE AZIMUTHAL ANGLE DISTRIBUTIONS OF CHARGED PARTICLES HAVE BEEN FITTED BY : D(N)/D(PHI)=N *(1+CONST(Q=1)*COS(PHI)+CONST(Q=2)*COS(2*PHI)), WHERE PHI IS THEAZIMUTHAL ANGLE OF CHARGED PARTICLE RELATIVE TO THE FOLLOWING COORDINATE SYSTEM : Z AXIS DIRECTED ALONG BEAM MOMENTUM, X AXIS DIRECTED ALONG TRANSVERSE MOMENTU M CONSTRUCTED FROM TRANSVERSE MOMENTA OF THE FINAL STATE PARTICLES (SEE PAPER). A systematic error of 0.03 has been estimated for CONST(Q=1) and CONST(Q= 2).\n",
